# The functions of the start sites that still build a start, or name a
# folder's program keys, outside the start plan.  Checked by
# tests/check-start-plan.sh.
#
#   file|function|count|pass|reason
#
# "count" is the number of matching lines' matches in the function; it may
# only fall.  "pass" is the pass that moves the function into a plan:
#   P0c-3   Run, Make, scripts, the shell, install lines, File > Execute,
#           the language servers, and the short commands (print, man)
#   P0c-4   the assistant's read grants (IncludePath)
#   plan    converted: the function hands its words and paths to its
#           action's plan (wpe_startplan_start takes only words the judged plan
#           holds; wpe_startplan_remove removes only what it allows), or it
#           reads an output's time for the editor's own up-to-date test
#   keep    not a start: a dialog that edits a value, a default, the
#           project file being written, the editor's own header reading,
#           a definition, a display table's slot
#
# On the tree this pass started from (1a9be21) the same scan found 62
# functions with 164 matches and no start plan at all; the check fails
# there (e_p_link_operands, among others, is no listed function).

# --- the F9 path: compile, link, project build (converted) ---
we_prog.c|e_comp_start|6|plan|the compile's words through e_exec_planned, its stale object through e_build_remove_stale
we_prog.c|e_p_make_link|6|plan|the link's words through e_exec_planned
we_prog.c|e_prj_setup|6|plan|the project's compile and link words, judged by e_prj_approve, started through e_exec_planned
we_prog.c|e_prj_compile_file|5|plan|a project file's compile through e_exec_planned, its stale object through e_build_remove_stale
we_prog.c|e_make_library|3|plan|ar through e_exec_planned
we_prog.c|e_prj_insert|2|plan|hands the library and object to e_make_library
we_prog.c|e_prj_link_arg|2|plan|an object onto the link line, a path of the plan
we_prog.c|e_prj_finish|1|plan|LDFLAGS onto the link line, words of the plan
we_prog.c|e_prj_object_name|4|plan|the object's path through e_prj_object_of, as the plan names it
we_prog.c|e_prj_object_base|3|plan|reads the object's name for the library test
we_prog.c|e_prj_inserted_after_compile|3|plan|reads the object's name for the library test
we_prog.c|e_prj_is_program_object|3|plan|reads the object's name for the library test
we_prog.c|e_prj_object_current|1|plan|the editor's own up-to-date test of an object
we_prog.c|e_p_make_note_program_current|1|plan|the "nothing to build" line names the program
we_prog.c|e_build_plan_approve|1|plan|the build's plan reads the output folder
we_prog.c|e_prj_approve|1|plan|the project's plan reads the output folder
we_prog.c|e_build_take_own_exedir|5|plan|"Use mine" puts the user's own output folder in force
we_prog.c|e_prog_take_own|3|plan|"Use mine" puts the user's own compile line in force

# --- Run, Make, scripts, the shell, install lines (P0c-3) ---
we_prog.c|e_run_program|8|P0c-3|Run's shell line joins Exedir, the program and Arguments
we_prog.c|e_run_start|3|P0c-3|Run's child spec
we_prog.c|e_run_start_text|3|P0c-3|Run's child spec, without a terminal
we_prog.c|e_run_sh|6|P0c-3|a script's shell line with Arguments
we_prog.c|e_exec_make|2|P0c-3|make with Arguments
we_prog.c|e_build_spec|1|P0c-3|Make's child spec
we_prog.c|e_exec_inf|1|P0c-3|starts Make's child
we_prog.c|e_shell_run|1|P0c-3|the shell's child spec
we_prog.c|e_shell_start|2|P0c-3|the shell's child spec
we_prog.c|e_system|2|P0c-3|a script on the console
we_prog.c|e_install_lines_run|1|P0c-3|a project's install lines through the shell
we_fl_unix.c|WpeShell|1|P0c-3|File > Shell
we_fl_unix.c|WpeHandleFileManager|1|P0c-3|the file manager's Execute hands a file name to the shell
we_term.c|e_t_system|1|P0c-3|the console's shell entry
we_xterm.c|e_x_system|1|P0c-3|the graphical editors' shell entry
we_lsp.c|lsp_spawn|3|P0c-3|a language server's child spec

# --- the debuggers (converted) ---
we_debug.c|e_d_arguments|1|plan|reads Arguments once for the debugger's start plan and its run command
we_debug.c|e_d_pick_start_arg|1|plan|the program's name, handed to the debugger's plan as its operand with its origin
we_debug.c|e_start_debug|1|plan|a project's program, handed to the debugger's plan as its operand

# --- the assistant's read grants (P0c-4) ---
we_ai_ws.c|ws_collect_read_grants|1|P0c-4|a folder's IncludePath widens the assistant's reads

# --- not starts ---
we_prog.c|e_add_arg|1|keep|the definition
we_prog.c|e_make_arg|1|keep|the definition
we_prog.c|e_ini_prog|9|keep|the built-in defaults
we_prog.c|e_arguments|8|keep|the Arguments dialog edits the value
we_prog.c|e_make_prj_opt|8|keep|Project-Options edits the values
we_prog.c|e_project_options|4|keep|Project-Options edits the values
we_prog.c|e_run_c_options|4|keep|the Compiler dialog edits the values
we_prog.c|e_prog_fields_of|1|keep|the Compiler dialog compares the values
we_prog.c|e_prog_note_typed_compile|1|keep|a value the user typed counts as his
we_prog.c|e_wrt_prj_fl|1|keep|the project file being written
we_progn.c|e_program_opt|12|keep|Programming-Options edits the values
we_progn.c|e_find_def|1|keep|the editor reads headers along IncludePath for its own header tracking
we_term.c|WpeDllInit|1|keep|the console fills its shell slot
we_xterm.c|WpeDllInit|1|keep|the graphical editors fill their shell slot
